[background arg="res://Temp Assets/Stockholm-Public-Library-Alamy-1808398246.jpg" fade="0.0"]
join Lizzy (Talking) right
Lizzy: VALERIE!
join Valerie (Talking) left
Valerie: Ah, Elizabeth, how was your last day of highschool?
Lizzy: You said that yesterday.
Valerie: Oh. Did I? I think I would remember something like that.
Lizzy: You also mentioned something about faxing me class lists. It was a bad day in all honesty.
Valerie: ...
Valerie: Hm. You are under a lot of stress, so it makes sense that you would feel overwhelmed by—
Lizzy: No, you don’t understand.
Lizzy: I’m reliving the same day over again.
Lizzy: All exactly the same.
Lizzy: Maybe not exactly the same. There’s little differences.
Lizzy: It’s like im stuck in some sort of...
Lizzy: Loop of...
Lizzy: Time.
Valerie: ...
Valerie: A time loop?
Lizzy: Yes! That’s the word.
Valerie: Time loops are incredibly rare, Elizabeth.
Valerie: Perhaps a more accurate word would be Deja vu? The sensation of feeling you’ve lived the same experience—
Lizzy: I know what deja vu is and this is  not it.
Lizzy: I’m experiencing the same twenty-four hours over again.
Valerie: Wouldn’t a time loop need to be repeated multiple times for you to know for sure that you’re in one?
Lizzy: Time loops are time loops Valerie!
Lizzy: Isn’t it enough that I’ve experienced the same day more than once!
Lizzy: No one should go through that.
Valerie: I do think it’s concerning that you’re experiencing the same day, but a time loop?
Valerie: The Keepers often hold committee meetings about these supernatural phenomena,
Valerie: and they often result in quite a few fists flying.
Lizzy: Val, please, level with me. Somebody has got to be behind this!
Lizzy: Somebody like Lady MacDeath, she raised a bunch of zombies in the last yesterday and was cackling about some evil plan.
Valerie: One of the keepers, Humprey Egbert, the second, actually published a case study about this very thing.
do GameState.learn_fact("v_case_study")
VO: Oh no, she’s going off on one of her tangents.
Valerie: In the report he asserted that he’d been through more than ten years of the same day looping over and over again.
Valerie: It contained a very exhaustive list of citations and appendices,
Valerie: due in part because he had written it while being stuck in said time loop.
Valerie: The control group in this case was the rest of the world.
Lizzy: okay, well, how does this help me?
Lizzy: Can you call Humphrey up and maybe he can walk me through how he broke his?
Valerie: I detest phones, you know this Elizabeth,
Valerie: but in any case, we wouldn’t be able to.
Lizzy: Why not??
Valerie: He died.
Lizzy: oh.
Valerie: While on a sailing trip...
Valerie: The circumstances were quite mysterious and I’m still convinced he was murdered...
Valerie: No one will give me the funding to look into it.
Lizzy: This was a waste of time.
Valerie: Elizabeth, please know that I’m here to help with whatever problem you’re facing,
Valerie: but you need to be more realistic.
Valerie: Why would Lady MacDeath go to all the trouble to make a time loop when you could spend all of your loops figuring out how to stop her?
Lizzy: because she’s evil?
Valerie: How about you go home and get some rest before graduation tomorrow.
Valerie: And then, if you wake up tomorrow, or at the beginning of the day again, you can face it with a fresh mind.
Lizzy: thanks for the advice.
Valerie: ...
Valerie: I’m sorry I wasn’t able to give you the answer you wanted.
Lizzy: It’s fine.
Valerie: Here, take this.
set {collected_item_name} = "pocket_watch"
join Characters/Item center [animation="Fade In" length="1.0"]
do GameState.pick_up_item("pocket_watch")
[wait_input]
leave Characters/Item [animation="Fade Out" length="1.0"]
[wait time="1.0"]
Lizzy: Your lucky pocket watch? Didn’t your grandma give you this?
Valerie: She told me it would get me through any difficult obstacle life threw at me. It’s made of gold and is only a few minutes behind.
Lizzy: why are you giving this to me?
Valerie: To give you something to remind you of how you aren’t the only one in this fight. You can give it back to me after you graduate tomorrow.
Lizzy: if there is a tomorrow...
do GameState.learn_fact("v_future_worries")


do ProgressionTracker.complete_requirement("1A", "library_dialog")
do GameState.mark_characters_as_spoken(["valerie"])
jump item_collected/